["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ibid", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Business Identifier (IBID)](https://ekys.org/business_identifiers/) is a verifiable unique identifier for legal entities as defined in the [ISO/DIS 25500-3](https://www.iso.org/standard/87705.html) draft standard. It is composed of three data elements: the International Business Registration Number (IBRN), the legal name, and the date of origin formatted as eight numeric characters (YYYYMMDD). Each element is separated by a pipe character (`|`) (e.g., `US-DE.BER:3031657|Code Management Association|19990420`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N6c101f1372d344a9958bef4ac8d65cae", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/fileKind", "globalId", "", ""]
["_:N15a295abc2984b208e885af053c18330", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/HashAlgorithm/blake2b512", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isni", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Name Identifier (ISNI)](https://isni.org/page/what-is-isni/) is a unique identifier used to distinguish the public identities of parties involved in the creation, production, and distribution of media content. Standardized by [ISO 27729](https://www.iso.org/standard/87177.html), it consists of 16 characters\u201415 digits plus a final check character\u2014and is often represented as a URI, such as `https://isni.org/isni/000000012146438X`.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/builtTime", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTimeStamp", "globalId", "", ""]
